    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Smith & Butler Estates are delighted to present this elegant two-storey-over-basement Georgian period residence to the Dublin 6 property market.\r\n\r\nThis rare property, situated on one of Dublin’s most desirable residential roads, offers exceptional potential for refurbishment, extension or future development, subject to the necessary planning permission. Occupying a substantial 0.70-acre site, the property presents an exciting opportunity for a discerning purchaser seeking a prestigious family home, investment or development opportunity.\r\n\r\nRetaining many of its original period features, the residence benefits from extensive private off-street parking to the front, with vehicular access to the side leading through to the large rear garden. The handsome façade features intricate brick detailing, original-style windows and an attractive decorative gable with ornamental detailing, creating a striking and distinctive presence.\r\n\r\nInternally, the generous accommodation extends to approximately 659 sq. m., with well-proportioned reception rooms, high ceilings, original staircases and large windows allowing excellent natural light throughout. The substantial site also offers considerable scope for extension and redevelopment, subject to planning, while the broad front driveway provides exceptional parking provision for a Dublin 6 property.\r\n\r\nThe mature gardens and surrounding greenery provide a wonderful sense of privacy and tranquillity, despite the property’s convenient position within one of Dublin’s most established and sought-after residential districts. The location offers easy access to a superb selection of amenities, highly regarded schools, public transport links, cafés, restaurants and some of the city’s finest parks.\r\n\r\nThis is a truly rare opportunity to acquire a substantial Georgian residence combining period character, an exceptional site and significant future potential, in one of Dublin 6’s most prestigious locations."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Room - 12.89m (42'3\") x 9.84m (32'3\")\r\nLarge principal hall-like space with high ceilings, timber floor and multiple glazed doors opening to the rear, ideal as main reception or studio.\r\n\r\nRoom - 7.26m (23'10\") x 5.54m (18'2\")\r\nGenerous front room with tall sash-style windows overlooking the mature front garden, suitable as reception or office.\r\n\r\nRoom - 3.39m (11'1\") x 3.58m (11'9\")\r\nBright room accessed from the hall, currently used as office space with period window detailing.\r\n\r\nRoom - 3.39m (11'1\") x 3.15m (10'4\")\r\nCompact room off the main corridor, ideal for storage or small study.\r\n\r\nRoom - 7.26m (23'10\") x 5.54m (18'2\")\r\nRear ground-floor space with large window and timber flooring, suited to classroom, living or workroom.\r\n\r\nHall - 7.26m (23'10\") x 2.24m (7'4\")\r\nImpressive entrance hall with decorative column, archway and stair to upper floors, linking principal rooms.\r\n\r\nHall - 6.24m (20'6\") x 2.33m (7'8\")\r\nInner hall connecting the period house to the later extensions and rear accommodation.\r\n\r\nBath - 2.33m (7'8\") x 1.74m (5'9\")\r\nGround floor bathroom with WC and wash-hand basin, off the side hall.\r\n\r\nBath - 2.33m (7'8\") x 1.74m (5'9\")\r\nAdditional ground floor WC and wash room convenient to reception areas.\r\n\r\nRoom - 6.24m (20'6\") x 5.84m (19'2\")\r\nVersatile rear room with direct access towards the garden, ideal for ancillary uses.\r\n\r\nRoom - 12.89m (42'3\") x 9.84m (32'3\")\r\nLarge multi-purpose hall in extension with extensive glazing and timber floors, suited to events or open-plan living.\r\n\r\nHall - 6.24m (20'6\") x 2.33m (7'8\")\r\nSide corridor within the extension providing access to further rooms and external doors.\r\n\r\nBath - 2.33m (7'8\") x 1.74m (5'9\")\r\nWC facility serving the rear hall and large hall space.\r\n\r\nBath - 2.33m (7'8\") x 1.74m (5'9\")\r\nAdditional WC off the rear corridor.\r\n\r\nRoom - 6.24m (20'6\") x 5.84m (19'2\")\r\nRoom in the rear wing, presently arranged as functional space with laminate flooring.\r\n\r\nRoom - 8.7m (28'7\") x 6.05m (19'10\")\r\nBright classroom-style space in modular block with multiple windows and vinyl flooring.\r\n\r\nRoom - 6.05m (19'10\") x 5.84m (19'2\")\r\nFlexible open-plan room within modular accommodation, suited to office or studio use.\r\n\r\nHall - 4.6m (15'1\") x 4.39m (14'5\")\r\nCentral circulation area of the modular block connecting several rooms and exits.\r\n\r\nRoom - 4.39m (14'5\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nMeeting or teaching room off the modular hall with good natural light.\r\n\r\nRoom - 3.2m (10'6\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nAdditional modular room ideal for office or consultation space.\r\n\r\nBath - 2m (6'7\") x 1.71m (5'7\")\r\nWC facility serving the modular accommodation.\r\n\r\nBath - 2m (6'7\") x 1.71m (5'7\")\r\nFurther WC adjacent to the modular hall.\r\n\r\nRoom - 6.05m (19'10\") x 5.84m (19'2\")\r\nLarge kitchen/dining-style space with fitted units and ample room for tables and seating.\r\n\r\nRoom - 4.39m (14'5\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nSmaller preparation or utility room beside the main kitchen area.\r\n\r\nRoom - 3.2m (10'6\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nCompact store or office space to rear of modular block.\r\n\r\nRoom - 5.84m (19'2\") x 4.6m (15'1\")\r\nPeriod first-floor room with large window and high ceiling, ideal as bedroom or office.\r\n\r\nRoom - 4.6m (15'1\") x 4.39m (14'5\")\r\nFront first-floor room enjoying views over the mature trees to the street.\r\n\r\nRoom - 4.39m (14'5\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nAdditional first-floor room currently laid out for desk space.\r\n\r\nBath - 2m (6'7\") x 1.71m (5'7\")\r\nBathroom with WC and wash-hand basin off the first-floor landing.\r\n\r\nBath - 2m (6'7\") x 1.71m (5'7\")\r\nSecond first-floor bathroom providing extra facilities.\r\n\r\nRoom - 5.84m (19'2\") x 4.6m (15'1\")\r\nRear first-floor room with timber floor, suitable for bedroom or study.\r\n\r\nRoom - 4.6m (15'1\") x 4.39m (14'5\")\r\nCorner room on upper floor with dual aspects, offering flexible use.\r\n\r\nRoom - 4.39m (14'5\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nUpper level room with period proportions, ideal as office or bedroom.\r\n\r\nRoom - 3.2m (10'6\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nTop-floor room providing additional accommodation under the eaves.\r\n\r\nRoom - 5.84m (19'2\") x 4.6m (15'1\")\r\nLarge attic-style space offering storage or potential for further conversion, subject to consent.\r\n\r\nHall - 3.2m (10'6\") x 2m (6'7\")\r\nUpper landing with access to roof spaces and top-floor rooms.\r\n\r\nRoom - 3.2m (10'6\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nCompact top-floor room suitable as store or small study.\r\n\r\nRoom - 7.26m (23'10\") x 5.54m (18'2\")\r\nDetached rear building room with generous proportions, offering workshop or studio potential.\r\n\r\nRoom - 5.84m (19'2\") x 4.6m (15'1\")\r\nSecondary room in detached rear block, suitable for office or ancillary use.\r\n\r\nRoom - 4.6m (15'1\") x 4.39m (14'5\")\r\nAdditional room in rear block providing flexible space.\r\n\r\nRoom - 3.2m (10'6\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nSmall store room associated with the rear block.\r\n\r\nBath - 2m (6'7\") x 1.71m (5'7\")\r\nWC serving the detached rear accommodation."
      },
      {
